From 50fd8f60da4af74f74d5f5a99d56be9a55fcd36e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Count the episodes over each rail's bar, and never smooth
 a count

The review found that the CoP pages drew the pad rail's bar and the
reward band's edges against the signed per-foot mean over episodes, a
statistic neither applies to: toe and heel episodes, and the two feet,
cancel in it. On the stance4 control run s52, 7 of 10 full-horizon
episodes failed the 0.80 pad rail at 6,553,600 steps while the plotted
means read +0.14 and +0.11. Comparison pages also smoothed the counts,
which hid every fall and drew clean counts that did not happen at the
judged checkpoints.

- Reduce the rails' own per-episode numbers (max_sole_cop_fore_aft,
  max_foot_cop_fore_aft, max_sole_tilt_deg, max_sole_corner_lift_m) and,
  per declared bar, the full-horizon episodes over it
  (<rail>_over_bar, <rail>_over_bar_fraction), and the episodes with
  either foot's window-mean CoP outside the band's edges. A run without
  a band is counted against the edges the band runs share, or
  --reference-band. All of it is in the JSON and the checkpoint table.
- Draw the pad rail (mean and worst episode) against its bar on its own
  panel, the bar no longer on the signed panel, and the over-bar and
  outside-band counts beside it; the same counts for tilt and lift.
- Never smooth a count: one run's pages draw a point per evaluation
  (falls written beside them, the training-fall axis scaled past the
  start-up window); a comparison draws one strip per run, flagged
  evaluations outlined and every alarm marked. Continuous series keep a
  centred rolling mean, labelled in steps, with each evaluation faint.
- Colour per seed and line style per group, each run named at its
  line's end and alarm; J lines solid and labelled; the axes at fixed
  margins so a step falls at the same place on every page; 96 dpi at
  native width; plain ticks on the std pages' log axes.
- Std: solid lines only between adjacent periodic checkpoints, a dotted
  connector across longer gaps; one line per pair when left equals
  right; "std from N of M checkpoints" on the page. Actuator names only
  when the run's plant_identity.json physics digest is the checkout's.
- Captions from the data (episodes per evaluation, bars, band edges);
  the saturation flag and the whole-foot CoP's zero described as the
  code computes them; what the ledgers do not record, on the page. The
  last training window ends at its last episode. Duplicate labels are
  refused. PNGs are written atomically; the HTML title is the report's.
- Tests pin the over-bar count on a ledger whose signed means cancel,
  the band counts and the reference band, the cause fallback, unjudged
  rows, the final-mark row, the plant check, the std joins and the
  drawn bars, band edges, marks and strips.

Report only: no training, evaluation, gate, configuration, digest or
notebook change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SaBkeMs656WoyRyzgRDbH8
